# Browser HTTP editor acceptance examples. These calls use public httpbin.
# File declarations are plain text; keep real credentials in secret API variables.
@base_url=https://httpbin.org
@name=Avery

### Inspect parameters
GET {{base_url}}/get?name={{name}}&tag=api&tag=editor
Accept: application/json

### Format and send JSON
POST {{base_url}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"id":9007199254740993,"name":"{{name}}","items":[1,2,3]}

### Format XML body
POST {{base_url}}/anything
Content-Type: application/xml

<request><name>Avery</name><count>42</count></request>

### Multipart upload
# @body multipart
# Open this request in the API client and select a file before sending.
POST {{base_url}}/anything
Accept: application/json

### Binary upload
# @body binary
# Open this request in the API client and select a file before sending.
POST {{base_url}}/anything
